# claude: this fork never had a .gitignore at all - build outputs were
# neither tracked nor ignored (presumably no one had previously run a
# real build in a git-tracked checkout of this specific fork). Covers
# both the real-hardware build outputs (kernel.img/kernel.list/
# kernel.map/build/) and the additive QEMU-only ones (kernel-qemu.img/
# kernel-qemu.map - NOT kernel-qemu.ld, which is a real source file).
# Deliberately does NOT ignore kernel/initcode or kernel/font1.bin/
# font.bin - these are pre-built binaries .incbin'd directly into the
# kernel image and are meant to be checked in (see notes_arch_arm_pi1.txt).
#
# kernel/fs.img (source/fs.img before Phase 0) WAS in that list, and WAS checked in, until 2026-09-09.
# It is not a hand-made asset like the fonts: it is the OUTPUT of uprogs/'s
# own build (mkfs plus every UPROGS binary), and the Makefile now
# regenerates it on every build (see its "kernel/fs.img: uprogs-fs-img"
# rule) rather than trusting a committed blob to stay in step with
# uprogs/*.c. Same treatment as the sibling forks/arm-pi2. What the
# committed copy was hiding here: uprogs/ did not build at all under a
# modern toolchain (a C11 static_assert redefinition in mkfs.c, and CFLAGS
# that only constrained the assembler), and nobody could have noticed
# while the blob stood in for it.
build/
kernel.img
kernel.list
kernel.map
kernel-qemu.img
kernel-qemu.map
/kernel/fs.img
